---

## Lore

Rifts Earth is pestered by actual monsters, demons, aliens and mutants. Giant footprints, mutilated or missing livestock, eyewitness reports and photographs all prompt an investigation by Northern Gun''s small corps of Monster Responders, called in whenever a dangerous creature is thought to be living near human habitation or coming out of the woods to stalk livestock or people.

Part hunter, part soldier, part exterminator and part special forces, Monster Responders gas, poison, shoot, trap and incinerate monstrous menaces, and use heavy weapons to bring down huge Mega-Damage beasts. Units are on call around the clock, may need SCUBA gear or jet packs, and can call in an NG combat robot or tank unit for more firepower. They share information with the police and the LPO, and often lead IMCN Merc Soldiers in raids on monster nests and lairs. To the citizens of Upper Michigan they are respected heroes, more beloved even than NG law enforcement; most are citizens of Ishpeming.

Alignment: Any, but most are Scrupulous, Unprincipled and Anarchist. All official NG Monster Responders are human.

## Equipment

An NG weapon for each W.P. plus 1D4+3 extra E-Clips for each (heavy weapons may include rail guns, a mini-missile launcher, a plasma cannon, etc.), Vibro-Knife, regular survival knife, a suit of Northern Gun M.D.C. body armor of choice, gas mask and air filter, first aid kit, 1D4 fusion blocks, 1D6 hand grenades, 1D4 smoke grenades, 1D6 flares, binoculars, nightvision goggles, wilderness clothing, hiking boots, camp stove, 1D4 weeks of rations, clock/compass, portable tent and sleeping bag. May also have access to power armor and military vehicles for missions against particularly powerful and nasty monsters.

## Pay and cybernetics

Some Monster Responders work in specific communities and are on call at all hours; others do contract work or are paid per job.

Cybernetics: none to start. Many receive implants over their career, and bionic or Bio-System replacements for limbs and organs lost in the line of duty.
